WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.100 --> 00:02.560
[Disclaimer: Characters, behaviors, places, organizations, professions,

3
00:02.580 --> 00:05.040
and events shown in the series are entirely fictional,

4
00:05.060 --> 00:07.520
solely for the purpose of entertainment, with no intention to instruct

5
00:07.540 --> 00:10.000
or promote any kind of behavior; viewer discretion is advised]

6
00:10.130 --> 00:11.170
I don't understand

7
00:11.190 --> 00:13.520
why a feng shui master like you needs to change the house plans.

8
00:13.710 --> 00:14.910
So let's meet halfway.

9
00:15.000 --> 00:16.880
Whatever you can change,

10
00:17.110 --> 00:18.380
go ahead and do it.

11
00:18.790 --> 00:19.790
Okay.

12
00:20.080 --> 00:21.710
We won't have to see each other again.

13
00:24.420 --> 00:26.400
Green is a lucky color.

14
00:26.470 --> 00:29.840
Maybe you should carry something that isn't bad luck for once.

15
00:29.990 --> 00:31.800
Why did you bring me here?

16
00:31.930 --> 00:32.720
Scared?

17
00:32.810 --> 00:34.280
Why should I be scared?

18
00:34.440 --> 00:35.680
If you aren't scared,

19
00:35.910 --> 00:36.990
then let's head inside.

20
00:37.290 --> 00:39.080
Are you Soul's girlfriend?

21
00:42.520 --> 00:44.320
She's not my girlfriend, Mom.

22
00:44.440 --> 00:45.440
Yes.

23
00:48.180 --> 00:48.690
So?

24
00:49.120 --> 00:50.920
Yes or no?

25
00:50.940 --> 00:52.300
- No! - No!

26
00:53.720 --> 00:55.120
No, I'm not.

27
00:55.140 --> 00:56.760
I'm not her girlfriend.

28
00:57.000 --> 00:58.600
I'm just the feng shui master

29
00:58.620 --> 01:00.680
who works with Miss Architect.

30
01:00.890 --> 01:02.500
Oh.

31
01:03.060 --> 01:03.920
I see.

32
01:04.210 --> 01:06.900
I've never seen Soul bring anyone home before,

33
01:07.010 --> 01:08.250
so I think you're...

34
01:08.270 --> 01:09.000
Mom!

35
01:28.590 --> 01:29.900
Finally.

36
01:32.810 --> 01:34.600
I'd better hurry back.

37
01:35.220 --> 01:36.220
It's going to rain.

38
01:40.210 --> 01:41.700
I can give you a ride.

39
01:41.940 --> 01:43.390
My car has a roof, you know.

40
01:44.770 --> 01:45.770
Hey,

41
01:47.040 --> 01:48.510
I just don't like rain.

42
02:04.740 --> 02:06.620
Why won't you let me drop you off at your house?

43
02:07.810 --> 02:10.200
I don't want to answer my mom's questions.

44
02:10.220 --> 02:11.510
She'll keep asking,

45
02:11.810 --> 02:13.720
"Why don't you take a taxi?"

46
02:13.810 --> 02:15.010
"Who is that?"

47
02:15.410 --> 02:16.600
"So, you have someone..."

48
02:18.110 --> 02:19.290
Are all moms like this,

49
02:19.310 --> 02:20.880
always nagging?

50
02:21.960 --> 02:22.960
Did...

51
02:23.310 --> 02:25.200
you just laugh?

52
02:27.850 --> 02:28.560
Ahem.

53
02:28.760 --> 02:29.980
No...

54
02:30.050 --> 02:31.050
Ahem!

55
02:32.820 --> 02:34.190
Here.

56
02:36.190 --> 02:37.220
This is your payment.

57
02:38.760 --> 02:40.000
I don't want it.

58
02:40.860 --> 02:42.600
Just like we agreed.

59
02:43.250 --> 02:44.760
But the ride here

60
02:44.890 --> 02:47.000
wasn't part of the deal either.

61
02:48.400 --> 02:50.220
I don't want to hear my mom nagging

62
02:50.240 --> 02:52.300
about why I let you go home alone.

63
02:53.130 --> 02:53.780
Here.

64
02:54.460 --> 02:55.850
Then I'll consider

65
02:55.870 --> 02:57.920
the dinner your mom made

66
02:58.190 --> 02:58.910
and

67
02:59.130 --> 03:00.300
this delicious cake

68
03:00.910 --> 03:02.500
as my payment,

69
03:02.980 --> 03:04.540
so we won't owe each other anything anymore.

70
03:05.600 --> 03:07.280
Don't come asking me to pay you, then.

71
03:07.540 --> 03:09.120
I won't.

72
03:11.470 --> 03:13.920
Good luck with Madam Waen's project.

73
03:14.300 --> 03:17.040
If you want your work to go smoothly,

74
03:18.900 --> 03:21.200
try wearing the day's lucky color.

75
03:23.370 --> 03:24.370
Nonsense.

76
03:25.510 --> 03:27.130
Suit yourself.

77
03:28.120 --> 03:29.200
I'm leaving.

78
03:39.990 --> 03:41.600
I hope we don't see each other again,

79
03:41.800 --> 03:43.200
Miss Architect.

80
05:49.080 --> 05:51.760
Xinxin, you're back, dear?

81
05:56.900 --> 05:58.840
Whose car is that?

82
06:03.190 --> 06:03.900
That's...

83
06:05.120 --> 06:07.190
That's your car, dear.

84
06:07.510 --> 06:09.300
Well, Dad was worried that

85
06:09.320 --> 06:11.700
you've been working late,

86
06:11.720 --> 06:12.680
so he...

87
06:13.100 --> 06:15.210
wanted you to have a car.

88
06:15.570 --> 06:16.810
So he bought it for you.

89
06:18.180 --> 06:19.560
But if you don't want it,

90
06:19.590 --> 06:20.720
- it's alright... - I'll take it.

91
06:22.710 --> 06:24.480
What do you mean, dear?

92
06:25.010 --> 06:27.720
I’ll take it because it’s what I deserve.

93
06:28.000 --> 06:30.400
It's only right that he takes responsibility.

94
06:31.290 --> 06:33.000
But I'm not going to use it.

95
06:33.560 --> 06:35.120
I'm going to sell it

96
06:35.140 --> 06:36.710
and keep the money.

97
07:14.000 --> 07:16.080
[Korawitsueksa: Father's Day, December 5th]

98
07:32.700 --> 07:33.700
Mom.

99
07:33.720 --> 07:34.720
Yes?

100
07:36.000 --> 07:36.970
Mom,

101
07:36.990 --> 07:38.840
when will Dad come?

102
07:45.300 --> 07:46.510
Xinxin, my dear.

103
07:47.580 --> 07:49.410
Dad is busy today.

104
07:50.080 --> 07:51.510
He has work to do,

105
07:52.110 --> 07:54.560
so let me take his place for now, alright?

106
07:56.720 --> 07:57.720
But...

107
07:58.850 --> 08:01.900
my friends' dads were able to make it, though.

108
08:09.040 --> 08:11.120
Dad is really busy today, dear.

109
08:12.980 --> 08:13.720
Come on.

110
09:28.360 --> 09:30.080
Did you drop her off safely, dear?

111
09:30.100 --> 09:32.300
Whoa, Mom, you scared me.

112
09:32.920 --> 09:34.280
What's there to be scared of?

113
09:34.470 --> 09:35.910
So, how was it?

114
09:36.400 --> 09:38.230
I dropped her off safely,

115
09:38.250 --> 09:39.760
just like you told me to.

116
09:41.590 --> 09:42.320
Hey,

117
09:43.600 --> 09:45.780
you're really not Xinxin's girlfriend?

118
09:46.000 --> 09:46.920
Mom!

119
09:46.940 --> 09:50.160
I'm not dating every single woman who happens to be around me.

120
09:52.620 --> 09:54.880
I think there's something between you two...

121
09:55.980 --> 09:57.760
Something wrong, you mean.

122
09:59.880 --> 10:02.040
If you two didn't get along, why did you bring her home?

123
10:03.140 --> 10:05.170
Didn't you say a feng shui master and an architect

124
10:05.190 --> 10:06.560
are the perfect rivals?

125
10:07.780 --> 10:10.490
Well, if I'm the one watching this match,

126
10:10.690 --> 10:12.280
I'm definitely rooting for these two.

127
10:12.530 --> 10:13.710
Mom!

128
10:16.800 --> 10:18.560
I think next time

129
10:18.810 --> 10:21.810
we should invite her over for dinner.

130
10:22.180 --> 10:23.640
I think she's lovely.

131
10:23.710 --> 10:24.910
I like her.

132
10:26.010 --> 10:26.760
Mom.

133
10:27.010 --> 10:29.040
Whatever you're hoping for,

134
10:29.330 --> 10:30.800
you can give up on it now.

135
10:31.410 --> 10:34.040
Because I'm not ready to let anyone in right now.

136
11:12.510 --> 11:14.900
"How long are you going to keep shutting yourself off?"

137
11:16.960 --> 11:18.520
"Does one heartbreak

138
11:19.600 --> 11:22.200
really make you scared to love again?"

139
12:01.300 --> 12:02.480
"This cake is so good!"

140
12:02.910 --> 12:04.900
Can I take some home with me?

141
12:28.440 --> 12:29.940
[Lucky Colors 2026: Never miss a beat when you dress right]

142
12:29.960 --> 12:32.390
"If you want your work to go smoothly,

143
12:32.700 --> 12:35.120
try wearing the day's lucky color."

144
12:35.860 --> 12:37.410
If the project goes smoothly,

145
12:37.780 --> 12:38.920
it's because of skill,

146
12:39.260 --> 12:40.600
not the color.

147
12:45.600 --> 12:46.680
Or is it?

148
12:47.800 --> 12:48.800
Gosh.

149
12:55.400 --> 12:57.080
[JR CONSTRUCTION]

150
12:57.730 --> 13:00.400
I’m thinking of renovating a house into an office.

151
13:00.570 --> 13:03.210
But I don't want it to feel too strictly corporate.

152
13:03.400 --> 13:06.680
I want it to feel homey when they come to work.

153
13:07.400 --> 13:10.610
Maybe we should remove this wall section,

154
13:11.000 --> 13:12.510
so it will be more open

155
13:12.530 --> 13:13.930
and easier to see each other.

156
13:14.300 --> 13:15.600
Mm...

157
13:15.630 --> 13:19.010
But I want my employees to have more privacy.

158
13:20.000 --> 13:21.000
Mm.

159
13:23.510 --> 13:26.010
They say people who don't like open spaces

160
13:26.400 --> 13:28.200
are usually great at their jobs.

161
13:29.420 --> 13:32.200
Maybe they just don't want to be watched all the time.

162
13:32.710 --> 13:33.710
I see.

163
13:34.200 --> 13:35.680
Then let's...

164
13:35.710 --> 13:38.600
make this wall area more open

165
13:38.760 --> 13:40.420
so people can still see each other,

166
13:40.440 --> 13:41.510
but not too clearly.

167
13:43.200 --> 13:44.200
Ms. Mim,

168
13:44.510 --> 13:45.640
you can always disagree with me.

169
13:46.120 --> 13:48.440
I don't know much about this anyway.

170
13:48.530 --> 13:50.400
Maybe something I said

171
13:50.420 --> 13:51.610
won't actually work out.

172
13:52.950 --> 13:55.620
We don't design things just to win arguments with our clients.

173
13:56.100 --> 13:58.160
We design according to what our clients want.

174
13:59.760 --> 14:02.060
Do you do this for every client?

175
14:02.700 --> 14:04.790
Only for a client who...

176
14:05.040 --> 14:06.890
doesn't need too much explanation,

177
14:07.180 --> 14:09.090
is easy to work with, and gets it right away.

178
14:10.310 --> 14:11.720
I like this type of client.

179
14:22.920 --> 14:24.360
Let's get back to the project.

180
14:25.280 --> 14:27.360
I haven't even gotten off-topic yet.

181
14:28.920 --> 14:31.480
I'll draft the zoning plan and a rough concept,

182
14:31.500 --> 14:33.080
then I'll email them to you.

183
14:33.730 --> 14:35.100
Let's meet up instead.

184
14:35.300 --> 14:37.240
I don't check my email much.

185
14:37.380 --> 14:39.010
I'd rather meet in person.

186
14:48.480 --> 14:49.660
Ms. Lada.

187
14:50.600 --> 14:52.300
When you said

188
14:52.450 --> 14:54.760
you'd rather meet in person than read emails,

189
14:55.590 --> 14:57.480
did you mean just for business?

190
14:58.880 --> 15:01.400
What else did you want me to mean?

191
15:18.110 --> 15:19.920
Let's just say I'll reply to your emails

192
15:20.020 --> 15:21.600
as quickly as I can.

193
15:26.300 --> 15:28.600
Your lipstick color looks great on you today.

194
15:29.410 --> 15:30.440
So pretty.

195
15:33.110 --> 15:34.110
Thank you.

196
15:35.070 --> 15:36.180
See you then.

197
16:27.990 --> 16:28.630
What?

198
16:28.990 --> 16:29.990
What are you looking at?

199
16:31.120 --> 16:32.790
Shouldn't it be me

200
16:32.810 --> 16:34.890
who's supposed to talk to her?

201
16:35.910 --> 16:38.400
Because of your duty or because she's pretty?

202
16:39.210 --> 16:40.310
Well, both.

203
16:42.400 --> 16:43.680
Well?

204
16:45.300 --> 16:47.080
Nothing.

205
16:47.110 --> 16:48.810
Well, she came here to discuss

206
16:48.830 --> 16:51.800
- renovating a house into an office. - Mm.

207
16:51.820 --> 16:54.030
And... after I’m done with the draft,

208
16:54.050 --> 16:55.920
I'll send it to you.

209
16:56.240 --> 16:57.240
You mean the work?

210
16:58.590 --> 17:00.510
Yes, the work.

211
17:00.530 --> 17:01.880
What else did you expect?

212
17:02.010 --> 17:04.400
I thought you were gonna pass the client to me.

213
17:04.420 --> 17:07.550
But since you two get along this well,

214
17:08.300 --> 17:09.300
I don't need to step in, huh?

215
17:12.380 --> 17:13.500
Better get back to work.

216
17:19.220 --> 17:22.950
Or you can let me talk to her instead.

217
17:23.120 --> 17:24.390
I'd be happy to.

218
17:24.900 --> 17:25.880
Stay out of this.

219
17:26.280 --> 17:28.120
Just focus on finishing your own work.

220
17:28.500 --> 17:29.080
Alright.

221
17:37.390 --> 17:38.440
Xinxin!

222
17:39.940 --> 17:40.870
Oh?

223
17:42.390 --> 17:44.430
I just saw your new car.

224
17:44.450 --> 17:45.600
Did you buy it?

225
17:47.220 --> 17:48.020
No, I didn't.

226
17:49.020 --> 17:50.450
He gave it to me.

227
17:51.710 --> 17:52.390
And...

228
17:52.820 --> 17:54.120
you accepted it?

229
17:54.630 --> 17:56.000
Why wouldn't I?

230
17:56.410 --> 17:57.780
I'm gonna get my revenge

231
17:57.800 --> 17:59.610
by leaving him broke.

232
18:04.550 --> 18:06.130
Oh, Lada.

233
18:06.520 --> 18:07.800
- Hm? - Someone wants to see you.

234
18:08.390 --> 18:09.500
Who?

235
18:13.520 --> 18:16.210
Ta-da!

236
18:17.810 --> 18:19.600
Hi, girls!

237
18:19.630 --> 18:20.990
Nan!

238
18:23.610 --> 18:24.550
I missed you.

239
18:24.700 --> 18:25.860
Gosh, girl!

240
18:25.880 --> 18:27.640
You came back and didn't even tell me?

241
18:27.660 --> 18:29.320
Guess your friends don't matter anymore, huh?

242
18:29.910 --> 18:31.440
Come on...

243
18:31.700 --> 18:32.660
I've been busy lately.

244
18:32.680 --> 18:34.890
I was planning to tell you once I sorted everything out.

245
18:36.100 --> 18:38.080
But Xinxin couldn't contain herself,

246
18:38.100 --> 18:39.960
so she planned this whole surprise.

247
18:41.200 --> 18:42.310
Surprise?

248
18:43.160 --> 18:46.010
And is your offer to check the feng shui for my new company

249
18:46.030 --> 18:47.360
part of your plan, too?

250
18:47.970 --> 18:49.520
I was serious about that.

251
18:49.540 --> 18:52.140
It's a gift to celebrate your return

252
18:52.160 --> 18:53.330
and your new company.

253
18:54.300 --> 18:55.410
You're the best!

254
18:56.360 --> 18:57.400
Thank you.

255
19:06.590 --> 19:08.010
Hello.

256
19:08.400 --> 19:10.500
Is this Xinxin, the feng shui master?

257
19:10.800 --> 19:12.700
Yes, I am.

258
19:13.160 --> 19:14.700
Do you remember me?

259
19:15.890 --> 19:17.320
Well, you sound familiar.

260
19:17.590 --> 19:18.320
Oh?

261
19:18.510 --> 19:20.310
Let me give you some hints.

262
19:21.010 --> 19:23.120
I'm gorgeous,

263
19:23.140 --> 19:24.600
capable, confident,

264
19:24.620 --> 19:25.900
and I sing beautifully, too.

265
19:25.920 --> 19:26.510
Oh!

266
19:26.530 --> 19:28.050
My daughter is gorgeous,

267
19:28.070 --> 19:29.500
capable, confident,

268
19:29.690 --> 19:31.200
and she's an architect, too.

269
19:31.610 --> 19:32.560
Oh, and most importantly...

270
19:33.500 --> 19:35.720
she's single.

271
19:35.820 --> 19:36.950
Oh?!

272
19:36.980 --> 19:38.350
Auntie Tai!

273
19:40.300 --> 19:41.390
I'm glad

274
19:41.710 --> 19:43.480
you still remember me.

275
19:43.800 --> 19:45.910
Anyway, let me get to the point.

276
19:46.240 --> 19:47.400
Well...

277
19:47.420 --> 19:49.790
right now, I feel like my house

278
19:49.820 --> 19:52.080
is really gloomy.

279
19:52.470 --> 19:54.510
So, I want you to

280
19:54.530 --> 19:56.950
be the love of this home.

281
19:57.930 --> 19:59.410
Be the love in your home?

282
19:59.760 --> 20:00.760
What does that mean?

283
20:02.330 --> 20:03.200
Uh...

284
20:03.270 --> 20:05.800
Uh, well, what I mean is...

285
20:06.610 --> 20:08.880
I want to invite you over to

286
20:08.910 --> 20:10.400
check the feng shui of the house,

287
20:10.510 --> 20:12.910
boost its love energy,

288
20:13.110 --> 20:15.320
and maybe attract a partner for Soul, too.

289
20:15.880 --> 20:16.910
Uh...

290
20:16.930 --> 20:18.190
Are you free this evening?

291
20:18.210 --> 20:19.710
Let's have dinner together.

292
20:20.650 --> 20:22.700
I already have plans for today.

293
20:23.290 --> 20:24.600
I'm really sorry about that.

294
20:25.200 --> 20:26.760
Maybe some other time?

295
20:27.310 --> 20:28.700
Oh... I see.

296
20:29.100 --> 20:29.690
Oh.

297
20:29.880 --> 20:31.900
It's alright, there's always next time.

298
20:32.600 --> 20:33.890
Anyway...

299
20:33.910 --> 20:35.710
thank you so much for thinking about me.

300
20:36.510 --> 20:37.590
Goodbye.

301
20:42.210 --> 20:43.210
Who was that?

302
20:43.800 --> 20:44.260
Hm?

303
20:44.280 --> 20:46.300
Don't tell me...

304
20:50.000 --> 20:51.480
There's something between

305
20:51.500 --> 20:53.410
a feng shui master and an architect?

306
20:54.200 --> 20:55.610
Like a cat and a dog,

307
20:55.720 --> 20:56.920
water and fire,

308
20:57.010 --> 20:59.680
rivals turned lovers.

309
20:59.700 --> 21:02.030
Imagined couples become real couples.

310
21:02.390 --> 21:03.860
Gosh!

311
21:03.880 --> 21:04.750
Listen!

312
21:04.960 --> 21:06.290
Listen to me, girls!

313
21:06.700 --> 21:07.510
I'm all ears.

314
21:09.120 --> 21:11.620
Her mom invited me over for dinner.

315
21:11.640 --> 21:13.490
She didn't call me herself.

316
21:14.660 --> 21:15.400
Mm.

317
21:15.710 --> 21:17.310
Trying to win her mom over,

318
21:17.610 --> 21:19.290
you're a sneaky one.

319
21:19.580 --> 21:20.280
Sis!

320
21:20.460 --> 21:21.050
Stop it.

321
21:22.900 --> 21:25.710
If you two didn't get along,

322
21:25.730 --> 21:27.760
why did her mom invite you over?

323
21:28.010 --> 21:30.200
Unless she's trying to find her daughter a partner, right?

324
21:30.590 --> 21:31.480
Correct!

325
21:31.500 --> 21:32.500
Well an-a-lies.

326
21:32.520 --> 21:33.600
- "Analyzed!" - "Analyzed!"

327
21:34.200 --> 21:35.310
Aha.

328
21:36.560 --> 21:39.230
Well, I think what Lada said

329
21:39.250 --> 21:41.600
makes a lot of sense.

330
21:43.060 --> 21:44.720
Then I can tell you,

331
21:44.750 --> 21:47.610
her mother is bound to be disappointed.

332
21:49.080 --> 21:50.960
You don't like her?

333
21:51.060 --> 21:52.800
It's worse than that.

334
21:53.100 --> 21:54.600
If I had to date her,

335
21:54.750 --> 21:57.030
I'd rather date a dog.

336
21:59.420 --> 22:01.810
But you've already pictured...

337
22:02.200 --> 22:03.290
yourself dating her.

338
22:05.010 --> 22:07.400
So, you don't mind that she's a woman, right?

339
22:08.090 --> 22:09.720
It's not about that.

340
22:09.980 --> 22:12.260
It’s because of who she is.

341
22:12.460 --> 22:15.200
But if her mother is rooting for you this much,

342
22:15.540 --> 22:17.210
it can only mean that

343
22:17.230 --> 22:18.520
Miss Architect has brought women home before.

344
22:19.290 --> 22:20.890
This means

345
22:20.910 --> 22:22.900
she might have dated women before, too.

346
22:22.920 --> 22:24.440
Sis!

347
22:25.810 --> 22:27.310
Lioness...

348
22:28.500 --> 22:29.160
Huh?

349
22:30.300 --> 22:32.560
Isn't it a "lady-killer"?

350
22:32.670 --> 22:33.590
Yeah.

351
22:34.800 --> 22:36.140
Pretty much the same.

352
22:36.340 --> 22:38.390
Whenever Miss Architect was stressed,

353
22:38.610 --> 22:41.790
she'd ruffle her hair until it looked like a lion's mane.

354
22:46.180 --> 22:48.200
You said you don't like her,

355
22:48.240 --> 22:50.000
but you do care about her a lot.

356
22:50.100 --> 22:52.880
You even coined a word just for her.

357
22:52.900 --> 22:54.420
- Mm. - "Lion."

358
22:55.290 --> 22:56.410
Let me tell you.

359
22:56.440 --> 22:59.480
I'm calling it now...

360
22:59.530 --> 23:00.420
"Love...

361
23:00.440 --> 23:01.000
is...

362
23:01.020 --> 23:02.970
coming!"

363
23:02.990 --> 23:03.940
No way!

364
23:03.960 --> 23:05.370
Absolutely not.

365
23:05.390 --> 23:06.020
Why?

366
23:06.040 --> 23:08.180
I'll prove you wrong.

367
23:09.820 --> 23:11.320
I've seen it all.

368
23:11.340 --> 23:12.700
Those feng shui masters who claim to be so accurate,

369
23:12.720 --> 23:14.240
they're completely clueless

370
23:14.260 --> 23:15.650
when it comes to themselves.

371
23:16.810 --> 23:17.900
Nan!

372
23:18.390 --> 23:19.390
I'm telling the truth.

373
23:19.790 --> 23:21.080
Just you wait.

374
23:27.760 --> 23:29.810
We'll mainly focus on enhancing your fortune...

375
23:32.080 --> 23:33.450
The architects are here.

376
23:34.250 --> 23:35.850
Please invite them in

377
23:35.870 --> 23:37.690
so we can discuss the project together.

378
23:45.410 --> 23:46.510
Feng Shui Master Xinxin.

379
23:46.590 --> 23:47.320
Yes?

380
23:48.240 --> 23:49.390
This is Soul,

381
23:49.410 --> 23:51.620
an architect from JR CONSTRUCTION.

382
23:52.110 --> 23:53.160
Miss Architect?!

383
23:53.180 --> 23:54.180
Miss Feng Shui?!

384
23:54.340 --> 23:55.480
We're f*cked...

385
23:56.110 --> 23:57.000
Uh...

386
23:57.100 --> 23:58.790
Did you two know each other?

387
23:59.110 --> 24:00.000
Well...

388
24:00.270 --> 24:01.390
perfect, then.

389
24:01.410 --> 24:03.300
My project should go smoothly,

390
24:03.500 --> 24:04.930
since you two

391
24:04.950 --> 24:06.600
should find it easy to work together.

392
24:07.100 --> 24:09.090
Maybe they won't work together at all...

393
24:09.790 --> 24:11.060
Uh, what did you say?

394
24:11.080 --> 24:12.080
Oh.

395
24:12.120 --> 24:14.120
No. I didn't say anything.

396
24:14.320 --> 24:16.070
Yes. They work together really well.

397
24:22.930 --> 24:23.880
Soul.

398
24:26.810 --> 24:27.860
Goodbye.

399
24:27.890 --> 24:29.000
See you tomorrow.

400
24:29.140 --> 24:30.010
Mm,

401
24:30.030 --> 24:31.530
drive safely.

402
24:34.600 --> 24:35.540
Soul,

403
24:35.560 --> 24:36.700
we can't fail this, alright?

404
24:36.720 --> 24:37.470
Don't forget:

405
24:37.490 --> 24:38.300
"Work is money,

406
24:38.320 --> 24:39.200
money is work!"

407
24:44.300 --> 24:47.640
Are you the only architect in Thailand?

408
24:47.870 --> 24:49.650
Are you the only

409
24:49.670 --> 24:51.040
feng shui master in Thailand?

410
24:51.370 --> 24:53.300
Why does Mr. Mongkol have to hire you?

411
24:53.900 --> 24:56.760
Maybe it's because I'm a really good feng shui master.

412
24:57.130 --> 24:57.810
You think?

413
24:57.830 --> 25:00.520
Then I must be a really good architect, too.

414
25:01.700 --> 25:03.720
If you don't want to work with me,

415
25:03.890 --> 25:05.210
you'd better withdraw.

416
25:06.540 --> 25:08.400
Why do I have to?

417
25:08.680 --> 25:11.700
The deal was made when we were looking for the location.

418
25:12.010 --> 25:13.700
You're the one who should withdraw.

419
25:15.490 --> 25:16.810
I can withdraw from the project,

420
25:17.400 --> 25:18.760
but why do I have to?

421
25:24.720 --> 25:26.440
So, you believe what I say now?

422
25:27.190 --> 25:27.900
What?

423
25:28.810 --> 25:30.610
The lucky color of the day.

424
25:31.120 --> 25:32.200
Well, well...

425
25:32.240 --> 25:33.600
Dressed in all green, huh?

426
25:33.910 --> 25:36.320
Guess you don't need my inhaler anymore, right?

427
25:36.500 --> 25:38.040
It's just a coincidence.

428
25:38.490 --> 25:39.700
Wow...

429
25:39.800 --> 25:41.800
what a coincidence.

430
25:42.710 --> 25:43.480
Quit it!

431
26:08.970 --> 26:11.560
If you want your work to go smoothly,

432
26:11.910 --> 26:14.290
try wearing the day's lucky color.

433
26:22.130 --> 26:23.780
[Lucky color chart]

434
26:23.800 --> 26:28.790
[Friday: Green, Pink]

435
27:04.310 --> 27:05.700
Are you coming with me?

436
27:06.910 --> 27:07.910
I'm alright.

437
27:08.710 --> 27:10.540
It's the suburbs out here.

438
27:10.560 --> 27:13.000
By the time you get a car, it'll be raining.

439
27:15.120 --> 27:16.520
You're awfully nice to me.

440
27:17.560 --> 27:19.910
As a fellow human being...

441
27:20.900 --> 27:21.900
I'll give you a fair price.

442
27:23.030 --> 27:25.440
Then go back by yourself.

443
27:25.660 --> 27:26.510
Gosh,

444
27:26.800 --> 27:27.800
don't be stubborn.

445
27:27.930 --> 27:28.800
Get in the car.

446
27:28.820 --> 27:30.600
I'm too tired to argue with you.

447
27:36.210 --> 27:37.010
Come on.

448
28:03.950 --> 28:05.960
Your mom called me the other day.

449
28:07.570 --> 28:08.640
Hey!

450
28:08.800 --> 28:10.500
Hey, careful! What are you doing?!

451
28:12.830 --> 28:14.890
What's with the big reaction?

452
28:18.710 --> 28:21.280
Did my mom do anything to bother you?

453
28:23.310 --> 28:25.080
She didn't do anything.

454
28:25.150 --> 28:28.020
She just called to invite me over for dinner,

455
28:28.870 --> 28:30.610
but I already turned her down.

456
28:31.690 --> 28:34.200
Guess she's not buying that

457
28:34.220 --> 28:36.190
we aren't actually dating.

458
28:42.420 --> 28:44.310
What's the matter, Miss Architect?

459
28:47.300 --> 28:48.400
I'm...

460
28:48.720 --> 28:51.000
I'm sorry on behalf of my mom.

461
28:51.210 --> 28:52.970
I'll tell her

462
28:52.990 --> 28:54.690
not to bother you again.

463
28:55.600 --> 28:56.400
Hey,

464
28:56.960 --> 28:58.390
I didn't tell you

465
28:58.910 --> 29:01.000
so you'd go fight with your mom.

466
29:01.300 --> 29:03.120
I was just sharing it with you.

467
29:05.310 --> 29:07.720
But what my mom did was wrong, too.

468
29:07.980 --> 29:09.210
Actually, that day,

469
29:09.230 --> 29:10.980
I was going to tell you

470
29:11.000 --> 29:13.610
not to mind what my mom said

471
29:13.630 --> 29:16.510
or how she tried to set us up.

472
29:17.910 --> 29:20.410
You must have felt so uncomfortable.

473
29:23.710 --> 29:25.420
I didn't feel anything.

474
29:26.020 --> 29:27.290
You're overthinking it.

475
29:33.410 --> 29:34.410
So...

476
29:35.940 --> 29:37.680
what do you think about...

477
29:37.810 --> 29:39.600
people who like the same sex?

478
29:42.110 --> 29:43.700
Love is love.

479
29:46.100 --> 29:46.790
And...

480
29:47.910 --> 29:50.400
it doesn't bother you?

481
29:53.710 --> 29:55.600
For me...

482
29:56.110 --> 29:56.970
No, it doesn't.

483
29:58.100 --> 29:59.400
Hey,

484
29:59.610 --> 30:02.180
society has changed a lot these days.

485
30:02.910 --> 30:05.820
People are just falling in love with someone.

486
30:06.600 --> 30:08.290
It's not a sin or anything,

487
30:09.200 --> 30:12.100
but it has to stay within moral boundaries, too

488
30:13.010 --> 30:15.800
If it makes you happy and doesn't hurt anyone,

489
30:16.300 --> 30:17.890
just go for it.

490
30:24.110 --> 30:24.910
Well...

491
30:26.110 --> 30:27.190
I...

492
30:27.610 --> 30:29.400
used to date women.

493
30:31.100 --> 30:32.100
So what?

494
30:33.210 --> 30:34.000
I mean...

495
30:34.920 --> 30:36.800
doesn't that shock you?

496
30:37.520 --> 30:39.090
I would be shocked

497
30:39.110 --> 30:40.800
if you were a ghost.

498
30:41.510 --> 30:43.100
But you’re still human.

499
30:47.900 --> 30:48.890
Well...

500
30:49.000 --> 30:51.200
if I'm close to any woman,

501
30:52.200 --> 30:54.010
my mom often thinks...

502
30:54.610 --> 30:56.000
she's my girlfriend.

503
30:59.210 --> 31:00.440
Are we close?

504
31:01.890 --> 31:02.480
Uh...

505
31:04.110 --> 31:06.610
I mean, if I were around a woman,

506
31:06.630 --> 31:08.690
something like that.

507
31:08.710 --> 31:09.800
Oh.

508
31:10.110 --> 31:11.320
Mm...

509
31:11.600 --> 31:13.110
Even though you didn't tell me,

510
31:13.400 --> 31:14.960
I could guess

511
31:15.200 --> 31:16.870
that you're...

512
31:16.890 --> 31:18.210
a lioness.

513
31:19.090 --> 31:19.720
Huh?

514
31:21.220 --> 31:22.800
What do you mean by that?

515
31:31.300 --> 31:32.300
Hey.

516
31:35.210 --> 31:37.000
Hey, you.

517
32:17.490 --> 32:18.960
It's alright.

518
32:19.390 --> 32:20.580
It's alright.

519
32:20.610 --> 32:21.900
It's okay, it's okay.

520
32:59.370 --> 33:00.020
Hey.

521
33:03.330 --> 33:04.210
Hey.

522
33:04.780 --> 33:05.780
We're here.

523
33:11.800 --> 33:13.000
Are you alright?

524
33:16.400 --> 33:18.290
Thanks for the ride.

525
33:22.010 --> 33:23.190
You should get inside.

526
33:30.710 --> 33:31.710
Wait.

527
33:31.740 --> 33:32.390
Huh?

528
33:33.910 --> 33:35.900
I still don't know what you mean by...

529
33:35.920 --> 33:37.560
a lioness.

530
34:00.390 --> 34:01.100
Oh?

531
34:03.400 --> 34:04.110
Hey!

532
34:12.620 --> 34:15.190
I think you might wanna check your fortune.

533
34:15.420 --> 34:16.640
You might be in for some bad luck.

534
34:17.600 --> 34:18.600
What bad luck?

535
34:19.520 --> 34:20.410
Well, you see,

536
34:20.440 --> 34:21.230
it was raining,

537
34:21.250 --> 34:22.700
you couldn't get a car,

538
34:23.090 --> 34:24.400
and you also forgot your bag.

539
34:27.480 --> 34:28.000
Give me that.

540
34:29.640 --> 34:30.640
What's the magic word?

541
34:36.410 --> 34:37.720
Thank you.

542
34:38.710 --> 34:39.960
Say it again,

543
34:40.210 --> 34:41.590
like you mean it.

544
34:45.190 --> 34:45.830
Thank.

545
34:45.860 --> 34:46.710
You.

546
34:46.730 --> 34:47.480
Very much!

547
34:50.310 --> 34:51.080
Hey!

548
34:52.600 --> 34:53.280
Oh?

549
34:55.110 --> 34:58.700
Besides wearing the lucky color outside,

550
34:58.920 --> 35:01.090
do you wear it inside too, Miss Architect?

551
35:01.290 --> 35:01.840
Hey.

552
35:01.910 --> 35:02.940
Well, well...

553
35:02.970 --> 35:05.720
Who said it was just nonsense?

554
35:06.010 --> 35:07.680
What are you talking about? Nonsense.

555
35:08.080 --> 35:09.190
But...

556
35:09.900 --> 35:11.360
I think I saw it.

557
35:11.700 --> 35:12.910
So...

558
35:13.100 --> 35:14.520
let me check again.

559
35:14.820 --> 35:15.910
- Let me see. - Hey!

560
35:16.040 --> 35:16.840
- Oh?! - Hey!

561
35:16.880 --> 35:18.220
- See? See? - Hey... Hey!

562
35:18.240 --> 35:19.440
What are you doing?!

563
35:19.660 --> 35:21.120
- I told you. - Come on!

564
35:21.600 --> 35:22.910
Hey, you!

565
35:22.930 --> 35:24.320
I told you it's green. See?

566
35:24.490 --> 35:25.160
Hey!

567
35:27.100 --> 35:29.140
Oh my, Xinxin!

568
35:29.160 --> 35:31.560
What are you two taking off?

569
35:32.680 --> 35:34.200
It's not like that, Grandma.

570
35:34.230 --> 35:37.160
I'm looking at her bra...

571
35:37.240 --> 35:37.970
Hey!

572
35:37.990 --> 35:39.210
Xinxin!

573
35:49.260 --> 35:50.460
Here,

574
35:51.190 --> 35:52.410
have a drink.

575
35:52.430 --> 35:54.000
- Thank you. - Alright.

576
35:55.220 --> 35:57.790
This is for my daughter.

577
35:57.810 --> 35:58.960
Thank you.

578
35:59.220 --> 36:00.600
What's your name, dear?

579
36:01.000 --> 36:02.090
It's Soul.

580
36:02.110 --> 36:03.270
Alright, Soul.

581
36:03.290 --> 36:05.160
What are you to Xinxin?

582
36:05.180 --> 36:07.820
- She's... - I'm asking her, dear.

583
36:10.680 --> 36:13.320
I'm an architect who's working with...

584
36:15.190 --> 36:16.160
Xinxin.

585
36:16.180 --> 36:17.880
An architect...

586
36:18.110 --> 36:20.490
Oh? Is this the one you...

587
36:20.910 --> 36:23.120
told me about?

588
36:23.140 --> 36:24.730
- Mom. - You said...

589
36:24.750 --> 36:25.400
Huh?

590
36:25.600 --> 36:27.480
That she's...

591
36:27.560 --> 36:29.890
Mom, you're just saying things.

592
36:29.910 --> 36:31.240
Oh.

593
36:31.410 --> 36:33.620
At first, when I heard about you,

594
36:33.640 --> 36:35.180
I thought...

595
36:35.400 --> 36:36.680
you'd be

596
36:36.700 --> 36:39.100
strict and outspoken,

597
36:39.130 --> 36:40.640
but you're not like that at all.

598
36:40.660 --> 36:42.410
You're even prettier in person,

599
36:42.430 --> 36:44.720
and you have the sweetest smile.

600
36:45.100 --> 36:45.810
Uh...

601
36:46.190 --> 36:48.320
Hey, I think my mom might

602
36:48.350 --> 36:50.920
have mistaken you for another architect.

603
36:51.110 --> 36:52.280
There are a lot of them.

604
36:55.900 --> 36:58.410
I thought she was your girlfriend.

605
37:00.000 --> 37:01.000
- Mom! - Hm?

606
37:07.420 --> 37:08.520
Have some milk.

607
37:08.540 --> 37:09.240
Thank you.

608
37:29.920 --> 37:32.040
I don't get it.

609
37:32.060 --> 37:34.900
Why does everyone have to think we're dating?!

610
37:35.010 --> 37:36.410
Like your mom,

611
37:36.510 --> 37:37.510
my mom

612
37:38.110 --> 37:39.450
and my friends, too.

613
37:39.500 --> 37:40.020
Huh?!

614
37:40.410 --> 37:42.650
You went and told your friends about me?

615
37:45.690 --> 37:46.690
Hey...

616
37:47.100 --> 37:48.030
you should head back.

617
37:48.410 --> 37:50.810
And I'm telling you right now

618
37:50.830 --> 37:53.120
to stay away from my mom.

619
37:54.700 --> 37:55.700
Even though...

620
37:56.080 --> 37:57.930
she seems to like you a lot.

621
37:58.000 --> 37:58.950
Gosh,

622
37:59.220 --> 38:00.520
you're acting like a kid.

623
38:00.540 --> 38:01.910
How old are you, huh?

624
38:02.380 --> 38:04.010
And how old are you, then?

625
38:04.220 --> 38:06.040
Hey, I asked you first.

626
38:06.800 --> 38:08.110
You tell me yours first,

627
38:08.130 --> 38:09.520
then I'll tell you mine.

628
38:09.540 --> 38:10.500
It's fair that way.

629
38:12.790 --> 38:13.920
I'm 29.

630
38:15.060 --> 38:16.570
- You're old... - Hey, you!

631
38:18.100 --> 38:19.860
I'm 25.

632
38:21.010 --> 38:22.430
You look like you're in your 30s.

633
38:23.200 --> 38:24.560
That's too much.

634
38:24.720 --> 38:26.010
Just kidding.

635
38:28.420 --> 38:29.420
With a mouth like that,

636
38:29.660 --> 38:32.190
you’ll never find a partner in this lifetime.

637
38:32.900 --> 38:34.100
With a face like that,

638
38:34.130 --> 38:35.560
you'll probably be single for life.

639
38:35.580 --> 38:37.000
Nobody could stand you.

640
38:38.310 --> 38:40.250
I just don't want anyone yet.

641
38:41.590 --> 38:43.160
You're still single, then?

642
38:45.220 --> 38:45.990
Hey...

643
38:46.170 --> 38:47.280
are you trying to fish for info?

644
38:47.940 --> 38:49.470
I don't have to do that.

645
38:49.490 --> 38:51.400
It's obvious no one would hit on you.

646
38:54.130 --> 38:55.190
You should head back now.

647
38:55.400 --> 38:56.710
Come on, go.

648
38:59.750 --> 39:02.020
Bye. See you again.

649
39:02.760 --> 39:03.910
What did you just say?

650
39:05.410 --> 39:07.010
I said that so I wouldn't jinx it.

651
39:10.100 --> 39:11.100
Oh...

652
39:11.400 --> 39:12.620
See you again, then.

653
39:13.710 --> 39:15.120
But I mean it.

654
39:15.410 --> 39:16.410
I'm being serious.

655
40:09.500 --> 40:10.500
- Soul! - Soul!

656
40:10.700 --> 40:11.910
Whoa, what?

657
40:12.310 --> 40:13.910
I should've asked you that instead.

658
40:14.100 --> 40:16.360
I've seen you fiddling with your phone for a while.

659
40:16.380 --> 40:17.400
Right.

660
40:17.420 --> 40:19.670
Is there a problem with Madam Waen?

661
40:19.980 --> 40:20.980
Please,

662
40:21.190 --> 40:23.200
don't mention her name here.

663
40:23.420 --> 40:25.300
It's traumatizing.

664
40:29.190 --> 40:30.190
Who's that?

665
40:30.540 --> 40:31.720
"Topknot Kuman."

666
40:33.490 --> 40:34.500
Keep your nose out of it!

667
40:37.310 --> 40:38.610
Sh*t! I'm screwed.

668
40:42.140 --> 40:42.690
Oh?

669
40:43.260 --> 40:45.400
You wanted to talk to me, but you just called and hung up?

670
40:57.100 --> 40:58.420
You two, leave for now.

671
40:59.010 --> 40:59.690
But we're about to...

672
40:59.710 --> 41:01.370
That can wait. Leave for now.

673
41:01.390 --> 41:02.000
Me, too?

674
41:02.020 --> 41:02.790
Yeah!

675
41:02.810 --> 41:04.470
- Huh? - What?

676
41:04.490 --> 41:05.100
Hey.

677
41:06.180 --> 41:07.590
Leave, both of you.

678
41:07.800 --> 41:08.500
Alright.

679
41:10.210 --> 41:11.510
Okay.

680
41:11.850 --> 41:14.100
- And when should I... - Leave, Oyl.

681
41:14.120 --> 41:14.920
Understood.

682
41:15.600 --> 41:16.950
Come on, let's go.

683
41:21.300 --> 41:22.300
Hello.

684
41:23.100 --> 41:24.100
Miss Architect.

685
41:24.120 --> 41:26.010
You wanted to talk to me, but you just called and hung up?

686
41:26.030 --> 41:28.210
Times have changed, Miss.

687
41:28.240 --> 41:30.470
No one uses prepaid phone cards

688
41:30.490 --> 41:31.720
and worries about using up their credit by calling.

689
41:31.740 --> 41:35.340
These days, even monthly plans let you prepay by the hour.

690
41:35.400 --> 41:36.900
What era were you born in, huh?

691
41:38.220 --> 41:38.910
Hey.

692
41:39.700 --> 41:40.610
My finger slipped.

693
41:41.940 --> 41:42.610
What?

694
41:42.970 --> 41:44.960
So I'm wasting my time calling you back?

695
41:46.210 --> 41:47.590
Are you free right now?

696
41:48.290 --> 41:50.040
I'll make it worth your time.

697
41:51.120 --> 41:52.110
What now?

698
41:53.420 --> 41:54.140
Well...

699
41:54.700 --> 41:57.000
I want to discuss Mr. Mongkol's project with you.

700
42:00.620 --> 42:02.090
I'm free.

701
42:02.300 --> 42:03.810
I just finished work, actually.

702
42:04.350 --> 42:05.910
But...

703
42:05.930 --> 42:07.910
I still can't find a ride home.

704
42:08.090 --> 42:09.490
Are you free, Miss Architect?

705
42:09.950 --> 42:11.000
Can you come pick me up?

706
42:11.820 --> 42:12.820
Where?

707
42:13.700 --> 42:14.900
Pathum Thani.

708
42:25.010 --> 42:26.890
Hello, Miss Architect.

709
42:27.090 --> 42:28.280
We meet again.

710
42:28.850 --> 42:31.390
Didn't you say you were just trying not to jinx it?

711
42:31.410 --> 42:33.290
Then why do we have to meet again today?

712
42:34.200 --> 42:36.840
I didn't think you'd actually come pick me up.

713
42:37.210 --> 42:38.800
You're lucky

714
42:38.820 --> 42:40.400
I happen to work around here.

715
42:42.400 --> 42:44.310
I guess I really am lucky.

716
42:44.330 --> 42:45.330
Because...

717
42:45.610 --> 42:47.310
I haven't even called a ride yet,

718
42:48.010 --> 42:49.700
and my chariot's already here.

719
42:50.070 --> 42:51.560
Did you trick me?

720
42:54.560 --> 42:55.800
What are you waiting for?

721
42:55.820 --> 42:56.820
Why not get in?

722
42:58.290 --> 43:00.420
Waiting for the invitation, I guess?

723
43:01.800 --> 43:02.800
Get in.

724
43:12.620 --> 43:14.920
Where are you taking me?

725
43:16.510 --> 43:17.900
You'll see.

726
43:20.300 --> 43:21.890
Do you like to surprise people?

727
43:25.180 --> 43:26.180
Well, a little.

728
43:42.440 --> 43:43.500
Hey!

729
43:44.870 --> 43:46.830
Did you trick me into coming to your house again?

730
43:47.350 --> 43:48.440
What did I do?

731
43:48.460 --> 43:49.750
You were the one who hopped in,

732
43:49.770 --> 43:50.550
don't you remember?

733
43:51.930 --> 43:54.070
You really are a lioness.

734
43:54.840 --> 43:55.710
Hey,

735
43:55.730 --> 43:56.620
don't be dramatic.

736
43:56.640 --> 43:57.940
My mom's here, too.

737
43:57.960 --> 43:59.300
And most importantly,

738
43:59.390 --> 44:01.300
I don't like you that much.

739
44:04.090 --> 44:06.300
I don't like you that much either.

740
44:13.210 --> 44:14.510
I'm back, Mom.

741
44:16.050 --> 44:17.380
Xinxin, dear.

742
44:18.900 --> 44:20.600
Hello, Auntie.

743
44:20.940 --> 44:22.100
How did you get here?

744
44:22.430 --> 44:23.090
Oh.

745
44:23.320 --> 44:25.960
Ms. Soul picked me up to discuss work.

746
44:26.050 --> 44:27.510
Hm...

747
44:27.970 --> 44:29.570
She picked you up?

748
44:30.730 --> 44:33.000
I just happened to be around there for work, Mom.

749
44:34.290 --> 44:36.710
But I thought you said you'd be in the office all day.

750
44:38.060 --> 44:40.500
I'll go upstairs to discuss work, Mom.

751
44:40.710 --> 44:41.680
Come on, let's go.

752
44:41.820 --> 44:43.500
I'll be going now, Auntie.

753
44:58.190 --> 44:59.780
I just don't want her to bother us.

754
44:59.810 --> 45:01.510
Don't mind her.

755
45:01.690 --> 45:02.690
I see...

756
45:03.290 --> 45:04.820
This applies to you too, then.

757
45:05.440 --> 45:05.900
Huh?

758
45:06.640 --> 45:08.390
Don't mind my mom, either.

759
45:09.000 --> 45:09.790
Gosh...

760
45:09.810 --> 45:12.210
I'm totally fine with it. Don't worry.

761
45:12.420 --> 45:14.280
Sit and wait here.

762
45:14.310 --> 45:15.710
I'll go get some snacks for you.

763
45:46.170 --> 45:47.170
What are you up to?

764
45:50.390 --> 45:52.070
You talk as if I'm a child.

765
45:54.100 --> 45:56.880
I was just checking your desk's feng shui for you.

766
45:58.500 --> 45:59.500
So, how is it?

767
46:02.000 --> 46:03.000
It's good.

768
46:03.420 --> 46:04.190
But...

769
46:04.390 --> 46:05.450
one thing's missing.

770
46:06.060 --> 46:07.320
A plant on your desk.

771
46:07.750 --> 46:09.800
Without a touch of green, your ideas get stuck

772
46:09.820 --> 46:11.290
and you lose motivation.

773
46:11.710 --> 46:14.790
You want me to grow a plant on my desk?

774
46:15.700 --> 46:17.930
I mean a small one.

775
46:18.230 --> 46:19.810
Like a golden pothos or something.

776
46:20.310 --> 46:23.210
Who on earth puts a tree on their desk?

777
46:24.220 --> 46:25.220
You're not exactly normal,

778
46:25.680 --> 46:26.950
you know.

779
46:27.900 --> 46:28.990
Miss Architect.

780
46:34.110 --> 46:35.490
And...

781
46:35.520 --> 46:36.590
one more thing,

782
46:36.790 --> 46:38.850
the number of lights in your room is odd

783
46:38.920 --> 46:40.900
when it should be even.

784
46:40.920 --> 46:43.260
- So you... - "Won't be unlucky in love."

785
46:44.110 --> 46:44.920
Am I right?

786
46:46.810 --> 46:47.810
Mm.

787
46:49.410 --> 46:51.030
If it's too much for you,

788
46:51.050 --> 46:53.730
you can just get a desk lamp.

789
46:54.200 --> 46:55.200
Why?

790
46:55.870 --> 46:58.600
It'll bring you luck in love.

791
47:09.990 --> 47:11.190
Can you guarantee that?

792
47:12.200 --> 47:14.400
You have my word as Xinxin, the feng shui master.

793
47:25.700 --> 47:26.980
I'll buy it for you.

794
47:27.000 --> 47:29.320
Consider it a good-luck charm from a feng shui master.

795
47:29.420 --> 47:30.230
I don't want it.

796
47:30.410 --> 47:32.530
It's not like I want to be in love that much anyway.

797
47:32.990 --> 47:34.440
It wouldn't hurt, you know.

798
47:34.600 --> 47:35.720
I'm free today,

799
47:35.920 --> 47:38.100
and my whole day is yours.

800
47:38.290 --> 47:39.190
Are you sure it will work?

801
47:39.200 --> 47:40.990
If the client doesn't like it,

802
47:41.200 --> 47:42.410
we'll all be in trouble.

803
47:42.840 --> 47:44.820
Can you stop sticking your nose in?!

804
47:44.910 --> 47:47.010
This is how the real world works!

805
47:51.100 --> 47:53.410
You're almost 30, dear.

806
47:54.700 --> 47:56.880
Just 30, Mom.

807
47:56.900 --> 47:58.990
If I'm still single at 40,

808
47:59.160 --> 48:00.530
then you can worry.

809
48:02.300 --> 48:04.000
But this girl

810
48:04.610 --> 48:06.200
is cute, though.

811
48:06.220 --> 48:07.360
I approve.

812
48:07.800 --> 48:09.720
But we don't know if she's still single or not.

813
48:09.750 --> 48:10.810
We'd better get the info first.

814
48:10.840 --> 48:12.200
What are you saying, Mom?

815
48:12.290 --> 48:13.820
We just met.

816
48:14.020 --> 48:15.500
How can you approve of her?

817
48:16.290 --> 48:18.840
Well, it just felt right.

818
48:19.010 --> 48:19.910
Oh?

819
48:20.370 --> 48:21.300
Should I...

820
48:21.800 --> 48:23.410
reach out to the official page directly?

821
48:23.510 --> 48:26.660
Hey, don't do that! It's embarrassing!

822
48:26.790 --> 48:27.830
Please don't, I'm begging you.

823
48:27.850 --> 48:29.000
Don't do something like that.

824
48:29.200 --> 48:30.290
Let me tell you,

825
48:30.510 --> 48:33.320
the days of waiting for someone to confess their love are over.

826
48:33.340 --> 48:35.110
Should I love her, or should I not?

827
48:35.440 --> 48:36.440
That won't do.

828
48:36.610 --> 48:37.800
You've got to make a move,

829
48:37.820 --> 48:38.500
get her info,

830
48:38.520 --> 48:39.050
and find out

831
48:39.070 --> 48:40.680
if she's taken.

832
48:42.200 --> 48:43.310
And if she's single,

833
48:43.800 --> 48:44.960
seal the deal for me, okay?

834
48:46.020 --> 48:47.020
Mom...

835
48:49.000 --> 48:50.620
I'm serious.

836
48:54.100 --> 48:55.100
Soul.

837
48:56.810 --> 48:59.220
How long are you going to keep shutting yourself off?

838
49:01.300 --> 49:02.810
Does one heartbreak

839
49:03.990 --> 49:06.690
really make you scared to love again?

840
49:17.920 --> 49:19.400
Give it a chance.
